allwinner-sun8i-emac: flush queued frames whenever the receiver is ready

A frame that arrives while the receiver cannot take it (RX not enabled
yet, or no free descriptor) is queued, and the backend (tap, socket)
stops reading until the queue is flushed.  The model flushed only on
writes to BASIC_CTL1 and RX_CTL1, but Linux drivers enable reception
through RX_CTL0 after RX_CTL1: on a bridged tap, where the host sends
traffic (IPv6, mDNS, STP) before the interface is up, the first such
frame stalled reception for good -- the guest's ARP requests went out,
the replies never came in.  User-mode networking sends nothing unasked,
which hid it.  Flush after every register write that leaves the
receiver ready.

---
diff --git a/hw/net/allwinner-sun8i-emac.c b/hw/net/allwinner-sun8i-emac.c
--- a/hw/net/allwinner-sun8i-emac.c
+++ b/hw/net/allwinner-sun8i-emac.c
@@ -775,6 +775,17 @@
                                  "EMAC register 0x" HWADDR_FMT_plx "\n",
                                   offset);
     }
+
+    /*
+     * A frame that arrived while the receiver could not take it was queued,
+     * and the backend stopped reading until the queue is flushed.  The
+     * receiver can become ready through several registers (RX_CTL0 enable,
+     * descriptors handed back before an interrupt is acknowledged), so
+     * check after every write.
+     */
+    if (allwinner_sun8i_emac_can_receive(nc)) {
+        qemu_flush_queued_packets(nc);
+    }
 }
 
 static void allwinner_sun8i_emac_set_link(NetClientState *nc)
